
All raw source datasets are published in Arabic by the **General Authority for Statistics (GASTAT)** and the **General Organization for Social Insurance (GOSI)** covering **Q1 2021 – Q2 2026**. This dictionary translates every filename, table structure, and recurring column header for non-Arabic readers and reviewers.

---

## 1. Core Consolidated Workbook (`Saudi Labor Market.xlsx`)

The primary workbook containing core quarterly time-series tables. Only active sheets used by the semantic model are loaded into Power BI; legacy prototype sheets from an earlier Q1 2025 draft were pruned during model optimization.

| Arabic Sheet Name | English Translation | Granularity / Structure | Description & Role in Dashboard |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `البطالة` | **Unemployment Rate** | Quarterly (Q1 2021 – Q2 2026) | Overall and Saudi unemployment rates (%) by nationality and gender. Drives macro KPIs, trend lines, and the Vision 2030 `7%` target tracker. |
| `نسبة التوظيف` | **Employment-to-Population Ratio** | Quarterly (Q1 2021 – Q2 2026) | Share of the working-age population currently employed (%), segmented by nationality and gender. |
| `أرقام GOSI` | **GOSI Registered Workers** | Quarterly (Q1 2020 – Q2 2026) | Absolute headcount of employed individuals registered under GOSI by nationality and gender. Powers total workforce KPIs, YoY growth, and nationality split. |
| `المشاركة` | **Labor Force Participation Rate (National)** | Quarterly (Q1 2021 – Q2 2026) | National-level participation rate (%) by nationality and gender, including Saudi female participation tracked against the `40%` Vision 2030 target. |

*Legacy sheets excluded from the final Power BI model:* `معدل بطالة الشباب` (Youth Unemployment), `المشتغلون` (Employed Relative Distribution), `المنطقة الإدارية` (Single-quarter Regional Snapshot), `الأجور حسب الجنسية` (Static Wages by Nationality), `الأجور حسب التعليم` (Static Wages by Education), `ساعات العمل` (Legacy Working Hours), and `المؤشرات KPIs` (Pre-calculated KPI Sheet).

