## 2. Standalone Annual & Single-Sheet Workbooks

Multi-year Excel files structured with one sheet per year (`2021`–`2025`) or a single consolidated time-series tab.

| Arabic Filename | English Translation | Sheet Structure | Description |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| `معدل مشاركة القوى العاملة.xlsx` | **Labor Force Participation by Region** | Annual sheets (`2021`–`2025`) | Quarterly participation rates (%) broken down across Saudi Arabia's 13 administrative regions, nationality, and gender. |
| `متوسط الأجر الشهري حسب الجنسية.xlsx` | **Average Monthly Wages by Nationality** | Annual sheets (`2021`–`2025`) | Quarterly average monthly wages (SAR) segmented by nationality and gender. |
| `متوسط الأجر حسب المستوى التعليمي.xlsx` | **Average Monthly Wages by Education Level** | Annual sheets (`2021`–`2025`) | Quarterly average monthly wages (SAR) across education tiers (No degree through Doctorate). |
| `متوسط الأجر الشهري حسب الفئة العمرية.xlsx` | **Average Monthly Wages by Age Group** | Annual sheets | Average monthly wages (SAR) segmented by age bracket, nationality, and gender. |
| `متوسط ساعات العمل.xlsx` | **Average Weekly Working Hours** | Single sheet (`متوسط ساعات العمل`) | Quarterly average usual weekly working hours (2021–2025) comparing Saudi and Non-Saudi workers by gender. |
| `التوزيع النسبي للسكان في قوة العمل.xlsx` | **Relative Distribution of Population in Labor Force** | Multi-period (`التوزيع النسبي لقوة العمل`) | Percentage split of the working-age population inside vs. outside the labor force. |
| `التوزيع النسبي للمشتغلين حسب مجموعات المهن الرئيسية.xlsx` | **Employed Distribution by Major Occupational Groups** | Multi-period | Percentage distribution of employed workers across standard major occupation categories (e.g., Professionals, Services & Sales). |
| `التوزيع النسبي للمشتغلين حسب المستوى التعليمي.xlsx` | **Employed Distribution by Education Level** | Multi-period | Percentage breakdown of employed workers by highest educational attainment. |
| `البطالة حسب المنطقة الإدارية.xlsx` | **Unemployment Rate by Administrative Region** | Multi-period | Regional unemployment rates (%) across the 13 administrative provinces. |

